--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Changes made to the Salesforce Canvas Framework SDK files
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The files above are modified versions of the SDK's src/main/java/canvas classes.
The upstream repository's LICENSE.txt gives the year as 2012; the source file
headers, which are kept as they are, say 2011.

All files
  - Moved from package "canvas" to "org.springframework.salesforce.canvas".
  - Changed the model classes (JavaBeans with getters and setters) into Java 17
    records: immutable, with accessors named after the components, such as
    userContext(), instead of getUserContext(). The setters are gone.
  - Removed unused imports and a stray extra semicolon.
  - Added Javadoc to every class, record and member, including private ones,
    which the build requires.
  - Wire names that differ from the component name use @JsonProperty on the
    record component instead of on a getter and a setter.

SignedRequest
  - Verifies the signature before the envelope is parsed. The SDK parsed the
    JSON first and used the "algorithm" it named to choose the HMAC algorithm.
  - The algorithm is fixed to HmacSHA256. An envelope that names another
    algorithm is rejected with a SecurityException; a missing algorithm and any
    letter case of HMACSHA256 are accepted.
  - Compares signatures with MessageDigest.isEqual (constant time) instead of
    Arrays.equals.
  - Decodes with java.util.Base64.getDecoder() (standard alphabet, strict)
    instead of Apache Commons Codec's "new Base64(true)". Malformed Base64 is a
    SecurityException ("... is not valid Base64") instead of being decoded
    leniently.
  - Uses explicit charsets: UTF-8 for the secret and the envelope text, US-ASCII
    for the signed text. The SDK used the platform default.
  - A null or blank secret throws IllegalArgumentException before anything else
    is read (as before, but checked first).
  - A missing or leading-dot separator is rejected. The error message no longer
    quotes the input, and the SDK's "Problem with key [<key>]" message, which put
    the key object in the text, is gone: the input carries the OAuth token, only
    Base64 encoded, so it must not reach a log.
  - Parse failures report Jackson's original message without the source text
    (the SDK used the full message).
  - Shares one static ObjectMapper and TypeReference instead of building them on
    each call. The class is final and has a private constructor.
  - verifyAndDecodeAsJson returns the envelope re-serialized from a Map. Its
    parse error names the right type (the SDK reported the TypeReference's own
    class).
  - No longer uses Apache Commons Codec, so the library does not depend on it.

CanvasRequest
  - issuedAt is a Long. The SDK used Integer, which cannot hold every value
    Salesforce sends.
  - The context component is named canvasContext (wire name "context"),
    accessed as canvasContext() instead of getContext().

CanvasClient
  - Added refreshToken.
  - The OAuth token component is oauthToken (SDK field OAuthToken), accessed as
    oauthToken() instead of getOAuthToken().
  - toString() masks oauthToken and refreshToken as [redacted] so a logged
    request does not write credentials to the log.

CanvasContext
  - Added the "application" section as applicationContext
    (CanvasApplicationContext, a new class that is not from the SDK).
  - toString() includes the Application Context section.
  - Accessors are named after the components (orgContext() for the SDK's
    getOrganizationContext(), envContext() for getEnvironmentContext(),
    linkContext() for getLinkContext()).
  - The environment is no longer replaced by an empty CanvasEnvironmentContext
    when absent: envContext() returns null.

CanvasEnvironmentContext
  - Added displayLocation, sublocation, referer and the "record" section as
    recordContext (CanvasRecordContext, a new class that is not from the SDK).
    The Dimensions record gained clientHeight, clientWidth,
    maxHeight and maxWidth. SystemVersion is now the record Version, with api()
    instead of getApiVersion().
  - Null parameters become an empty map, and the map is copied into an
    unmodifiable one. Null values are allowed.
  - Dimensions, Version and the record are nested records, so the SDK's
    "needs default ctor for Jackson" constructor is gone.
  - toString() is the generated record form. The SDK's toString() would throw a
    NullPointerException when dimensions or version was absent.

CanvasLinkContext
  - Added loginUrl.
  - The userUrl wire property is the component userProfileUrl, accessed as
    userProfileUrl() (the SDK's getter was getUserUrl()).

CanvasOrganizationContext
  - Added namespacePrefix.
  - The currency component is currencyIsoCode (wire name "currencyIsoCode"),
    accessed as currencyIsoCode() instead of getCurrencyISOCode(), because the
    SDK's property spelling did not match its own wire name.

CanvasUserContext
  - Added siteUrl, siteUrlPrefix, networkId and isDefaultNetwork (boolean).
  - The accessibility component is accessibilityModeEnabled (the wire name),
    accessed as accessibilityModeEnabled() instead of isAccessibilityMode().
  - toString() is the generated record form.

The new fields and wire names in this list were checked against requests from a
live Salesforce org (Lightning and Visualforce). The SDK has no tests; the
classes are covered by tests written for this project.
